===Speak with Castorice and Anaxa{{subst:void|<!--104020602-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to )
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
----
:'''Anaxa:''' It's fortunate we don't have to confront that woman while I'm hauling around this sick body. Castorice, and this friend I haven't gotten the chance to know &mdash; I'll take my leave for today.
:'''Anaxa:''' That Titan made a myriad of adjustments on their own... My head still aches from that. I don't want to stay a second longer in this noisy city if I can.
:'''Castorice:''' Please be careful. Okhema isn't the Grove. This place...
:'''Anaxa:''' ...Is covered by her golden threads, I know. That woman is extremely confident I won't escape her grasp.
:'''Anaxa:''' Don't worry. As I said before, I'll mind my behavior.
:'''Castorice:''' {{MC|м=Mr.|ж=Miss}} (Trailblazer), so many unexpected things happened on our journey to the Grove... We truly had no intention of putting you in danger, let alone face the black tide head on...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Trouble is my old friend by now.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We made it back alive. So much for the black tide.
::'''Castorice:''' Please do not underestimate the threat the black tide poses.
:'''Castorice:''' The black tide is not just an enemy of Okhema, but all of Amphoreus. Even back when the forces of Strife coveted the holy city, their warriors still undeniably halted the black tide outside Castrum Kremnos.
:'''Castorice:''' {{Rubi|Nikador's|Strife Titan}} Coreflame now sits vacant and the black tide has returned... The Grove is an academic city with the best understanding of the black tide. It shouldn't have fallen so easily, and yet it was taken overnight, leaving the city in blood and tears, haunted by the spirits of departed heroes...
:'''Castorice:''' The trial of Strife is imminent. I pray Mydei will be able to steel his resolve soon...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And that black-robed swordmaster...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The dreadful enemies of the Grove are also creations of the black tide?
:'''Castorice:''' Lady Tribbie once traveled across thousands of cities in Amphoreus to repel the black tide, but even they have no recollection of this powerful enemy in all their journeys. Perhaps the fall of Strife has triggered even more terrifying events in unseen places...
:'''Castorice:''' Lady Tribbie once traveled across thousands of cities in Amphoreus to repel the black tide, but even they have no recollection of this powerful enemy in all their journeys. Perhaps the fall of Strife has triggered even more terrifying events in unseen places...
:'''Castorice:''' As for me... I detected a strong stench of death from that entity, but it wasn't because he had a connection with {{Rubi|Thanatos|Death Titan}}... I'm afraid it's purely because he has sent countless others to their deaths.
:'''Castorice:''' Speaking of {{Rubi|Thanatos|Death Titan}}... {{MC|м=Mr.|ж=Miss}} (Trailblazer), there is something else I wish to verify with you.
:'''Castorice:''' You must have an idea of the... curse I bear by now. I was born as the Shadow of Death, a poison shunned by all living beings...
:'''Castorice:''' Yet when you caught me in the Grove...
:'''Castorice:''' ...I'm curious why you weren't affected by my power, {{MC|м=Mr.|ж=Miss}} (Trailblazer)?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I had totally forgotten about this until you brought it up.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Maybe it just hasn't taken effect yet?
::'''Castorice:''' That might be the case if we only brushed the very tips of our fingers, but back then...
::I'm used to it. I'm just special like that.
::Now that you mention it, I think the same thing happened in the Vortex...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm used to it. I'm just special like that.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Now that you mention it, I think the same thing happened in the Vortex...
:'''Castorice:''' My apologies for the abrupt question. For all my life, I've always wondered: What is my connection to death? And why am I inextricably linked to {{Rubi|Thanatos|Death Titan}}?
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

===Return to your private bath chamber and end this day{{subst:void|<!--104020603-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Dan Heng)
:{{tx}}
:'''Dan Heng:''' Long time no see. I've heard about what happened from Phainon... You've been through a lot.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Not at all. It's all in service to Trailblaze.
::'''Dan Heng:''' Heh... I wasn't expecting Amphoreus to temper the will of the Nameless.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Life is a struggle.
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...May you never succumb to the dark side of Trailblaze.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I missed you so much, my dearest friend!
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...It seems you took things pretty hard.
:{{tx}}
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What were you doing while I was gone?
:'''Dan Heng:''' I was organizing logs. I also asked Hyacine for some research material from the Grove.
:'''Dan Heng:''' I discovered something interesting. Do you remember that Amphoreus's sky was sealed away by a Titan? {{Rubi|Aquila's|Sky Titan}} presence keeps this world isolated from the rest of the world beyond the sky.
:'''Dan Heng:''' It seems Hyacine's ancestors were the Sky Priests who worshipped {{Rubi|Aquila|Sky Titan}}. Perhaps she can give us more clues to find a way back to the Astral Express.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Nothing out of the ordinary happened in the holy city in the past few days. I didn't have to talk to anyone either. It was kind of nice spending time alone.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Just you wait. Your good times are coming to an end!
::'''Dan Heng:''' After what happened at the Grove, there's sure to be unrest in the coming days. We should rest for now.
::Awful! I should have stayed and organized documents with you.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Awful! I should have stayed and organized documents with you.
:'''Dan Heng:''' ...I'm afraid you'd probably find the task of organizing just as awful.
:'''Dan Heng:''' You look tired. You should get some sleep before we set off tomorrow...
:{{tx}}
